s a digit and as lamps","color":"amber","style":"filled","fontSize":11,"carry":true,"width":56,"height":20}},"n_grp_scope":{"id":"n_grp_scope","type":"deco.group","position":{"x":880,"y":310},"params":{"title":"Waveform","subtitle":"Every stage halves the rate of the one before it","color":"purple","style":"filled","fontSize":11,"carry":true,"width":28,"height":20}},"n_note_sync":{"id":"n_note_sync","type":"deco.text","position":{"x":490,"y":730},"params":{"text":"### What synchronous means\nEvery flip-flop is clocked by the *same* edge —\nnothing is chained off a neighbour's output — so\nall four bits move at once and the readout never\nshows a half-finished number on its way from\n`0111` to `1000`.","format":"markdown","fontSize":12,"align":"left","color":"default","background":"none","width":32,"height":12}},"n_note_carry":{"id":"n_note_carry","type":"deco.text","position":{"x":840,"y":730},"params":{"text":"### What the AND gates are for\nA stage flips only when every stage below it is\nalready 1, and that is the one question the gates\nanswer. It is binary counting written out in\nhardware.\n\n**Power-on reset** fires a single pulse as the\nsimulation starts, so the chain begins from a\nknown `0000` rather than from `X`.","format":"markdown","fontSize":12,"align":"left","color":"default","background":"none","width":32,"height":15}}},"wires":{"w_gDUNWhp-PQ5B":{"id":"w_gDUNWhp-PQ5B","from":{"nodeId":"n_inPxO6QXHkqY","pinId":"out"},"to":{"nodeId":"n_3d2ZLdx50qcX","pinId":"en"}},"w_Slh2aF49SyX2":{"id":"w_Slh2aF49SyX2","from":{"nodeId":"n_eQKbQWUOcB5q","pinId":"out"},"to":{"nodeId":"n_2np_2mv4YDTc","pinId":"t"}},"w_slV_ShbRwgg9":{"id":"w_slV_ShbRwgg9","from":{"nodeId":"n_vRG3Yjq0qet9","pinId":"out"},"to":{"nodeId":"n_FU57Td6T6W0p","pinId":"value"}},"w_j9XsnhD4XMZL":{"id":"w_j9XsnhD4XMZL","from":{"nodeId":"n_AXQbdnsbFH98","pinId":"out"},"to":{"nodeId":"n_BBCY1xAd4vvP","pinId":"t"}},"w_TbUWcrFuWoef":{"id":"w_TbUWcrFuWoef","from":{"nodeId":"n_2np_2mv4YDTc","pinId":"q"}